---
// Restates the AutoMate app's privacy policy (automate-v2/docs/PRIVACY-POLICY.md)
// for the app as shipped on Google Play. The drive-recording sections in that
// file describe a feature that has not shipped yet; add them here when it does.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { APP_PRIVACY_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/facts';

const path = '/privacy/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | AutoMate car expense tracker"
  description="What the AutoMate app stores, what it sends and what it never does: records on your phone, no account, no ads, anonymous crash reports and usage statistics."
  path={path}
  ogSlug="privacy"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', path }]}
>
  <article class="doc wrap">
    <header class="doc-head">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the privacy policy of the AutoMate Android app, written out for this website. The copy linked from
        inside the app is at <a href={APP_PRIVACY_URL}>{APP_PRIVACY_URL.replace('https://', '')}</a>. If the two ever
        differ, that one applies.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your vehicles, fill-ups, services, expenses and reminders are stored on your phone. There is no AutoMate account or cloud copy.</li>
        <li>The app shows no ads and sells no data.</li>
        <li>It sends anonymous crash reports and anonymous usage statistics. You can turn usage statistics off.</li>
        <li>A VIN you look up is sent to the US government’s free NHTSA database. Nothing else about your car is.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data storage</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you enter (vehicles, fuel logs, service records, expenses, reminders and settings) is stored locally
        on your device in a SQLite database. There is no AutoMate account, cloud storage or remote database for your
        records. Your records leave your device only when you choose to export or back them up.
      </p>
      <p>AutoMate sends limited data over the internet only in these cases:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>VIN lookup.</strong> If you enter or scan a VIN (Vehicle Identification Number), the app sends that VIN
          to the free NHTSA public API to look up your vehicle’s year, make and model.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Install notification.</strong> Once per install, the app sends its version, your device’s OS and OS
          version, device brand and model, and language setting to the developer. It contains none of your records, no
          location and no personal information.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Usage analytics and crash reports,</strong> described below.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Usage analytics</h2>
      <p>
        AutoMate collects anonymous usage data through Firebase Analytics to improve the app: app opens and session
        length, which features are used (for example adding a fill-up or creating a reminder), screen navigation, and
        device type and OS version. It includes no personally identifiable information.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can turn this off at any time in <strong>Settings, Privacy, Share Usage Data</strong>. When it is off, no
        analytics events are sent.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Crash reports</h2>
      <p>
        AutoMate collects anonymous crash reports through Firebase Crashlytics to keep the app stable: stack traces and
        error details, device type, OS and app version, and a short log of the steps leading to the crash. Crash
        reporting is always on and cannot be turned off. Crash reports contain no personal information.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What the app does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No advertising SDKs or ad tracking.</li>
        <li>No user profiling.</li>
        <li>No cookies or web beacons.</li>
        <li>No data sold or shared with third parties.</li>
        <li>No collection of names, email addresses or phone numbers.</li>
        <li>No account: no sign-up, no login.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>Each permission is requested only when you take an action that needs it, never on first launch.</p>
      <h3>Camera</h3>
      <p>
        When you tap the camera button to photograph a receipt or your vehicle, or to scan a VIN barcode. Photos are
        saved in the app’s own storage. The camera is never used in the background.
      </p>
      <h3>Photo library</h3>
      <p>
        When you tap the gallery button to attach an existing photo. Only the photo you pick is copied into the app.
      </p>
      <h3>Location</h3>
      <p>
        When you tap “Use current location” while adding a gas station or service shop. AutoMate reads your position
        once and saves it with that place, on your device. It does not track your location in the background.
      </p>
      <h3>Notifications</h3>
      <p>
        When you create your first maintenance reminder. Reminder notifications are generated on your device; no
        notification data goes to or from a server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Export, backup and restore</h2>
      <p>
        You can export your data as CSV or PDF at any time, filtered by vehicle and date range. You can also back up
        your database to a file and restore it later. Both are shared through your phone’s standard share sheet, so you
        decide where the file goes. There is no automatic cloud backup.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        automateapp.info sets no cookies and runs no analytics or tracking scripts. It is a static site hosted on GitHub
        Pages, which may keep standard server logs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>AutoMate is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from children.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        When the policy changes, the updated version ships with the app update and the date on the in-app policy changes
        with it. Questions go to the developer at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
